git-svn-id: https://svn.apache.org/repos/asf/lucene/dev/trunk@1423932 13f79535-47bb-0310-9956-ffa450edef68

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by `NullPointerException` occurring when the `afterClass` method in `SolrTestCaseJ4` attempted to close the Solr core, specifically when trying to shutdown `defaultClient` or `loadbalancer` without checking if they were null, leading to an unhandled exception if either object was not initialized.

Here is the patch:

   @Override
   public void close() {
     try {
       ExecutorUtil.shutdownAndAwaitTermination(commExecutor);
     } catch (Throwable e) {
       SolrException.log(log, e);
     }

     try {
-      defaultClient.getConnectionManager().shutdown();
+      if(defaultClient != null) {
+        defaultClient.getConnectionManager().shutdown();
+      }
     } catch (Throwable e) {
       SolrException.log(log, e);
     }
     try {
-      loadbalancer.shutdown();
+      if(loadbalancer != null) {
+        loadbalancer.shutdown();
+      }
     } catch (Throwable e) {
       SolrException.log(log, e);
     }

   }
 }


